isease (MASLD) pathogenesis remains undefined. We identified selective lipid deposition in the pericentral zone during early MASLD. Multiomics analyses confirmed enhanced pericentral lipid metabolism in both hepatocytes and LSECs. Mechanistically, pericentral LSEC marker c-Kit transcriptionally activated FGF1 via nuclear receptor RXRG, which suppressed hepatocellular lipid accumulation through FGFR4 signaling. Retinoic acid (RXRG\u2019s endogenous ligand and active vitamin A metabolite) phenocopied FGF1\u2019s antisteatotic effects. Clinical data revealed an inverse correlation between dietary vitamin A and MASLD severity, suggesting therapeutic potential of vitamin A supplementation for early intervention.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1126\/sciadv.aed4384","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,19]],"date-time":"2026-06-19T18:00:33Z","timestamp":1781892033000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.34133\/aaas_crossmark","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Liver endothelial zonation orchestrates hepatic steatosis onset through retinoic acid\u2013regulated FGF1"],"prefix":"10.1126","volume":"12","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7235-1374","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Zhiqiang","family":"Fang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Hepatobiliary Surgery, Xi-Jing Hospital, Fourth Military Medical University, Xi\u2019an, China."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4203-5581","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Bo","family":"Che","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Hepatobiliary Surgery, Xi-Jing Hospital, Fourth Military Medical University, Xi\u2019an, China."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-8487-3738","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Yuwei","family":"Ling","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Hepatobiliary Surgery, Xi-Jing